; iter_non_vec_register_empty_slice: an ITER whose register does not hold a
; vec raises even when the slice is empty and the body would not have run.
;
; ITER reads its register whether or not the body runs, so skipping the
; loop without ever resolving the register drops that read.
; spec/xqvm/ISA.md's ITER row orders the steps register-read-before-skip
; and its error clause has no emptiness carve-out.
;
; The register is filled from calldata rather than by STOW, so its kind is
; decided only by what the caller passes. The program is admissible to a
; chain's store_program. A VM that skips the loop before the type check
; would halt with outputs = [7] here instead of faulting (as 0.3.x did).

PUSH 0
INPUT r0         ; r0 = 5, an int
PUSH 1           ; start_idx
PUSH 1           ; end_idx -- empty slice
ITER r0
NEXT

PUSH 7
STOW r1
PUSH 0
OUTPUT r1
HALT
